---Shared configuration applied to all runs in a batch. Fields specified in a per-run InlineSetting entry override the corresponding fields in this object for that run. The parameters and runTags fields are merged rather than replaced — run-specific values take precedence when keys overlap.
---@class aws.omics.DefaultRunSetting
---@field workflowId aws.omics.WorkflowId The identifier of the workflow to run.
---@field workflowType? aws.omics.WorkflowType The type of the originating workflow. Batch runs are not supported with READY2RUN workflows.
---@field roleArn aws.omics.RunRoleArn The IAM role ARN that grants HealthOmics permissions to access required Amazon Web Services resources such as Amazon S3 and CloudWatch. The role must have the same permissions required for individual StartRun calls.
---@field name? aws.omics.RunName An optional user-friendly name applied to each workflow run. Can be overridden per run.
---@field cacheId? aws.omics.NumericIdInArn The identifier of the run cache to associate with the runs.
---@field cacheBehavior? aws.omics.CacheBehavior The cache behavior for the runs. Requires cacheId to be set.
---@field runGroupId? aws.omics.RunGroupId The ID of the run group to contain all workflow runs in the batch.
---@field priority? number An integer priority for the workflow runs. Higher values correspond to higher priority. A value of 0 corresponds to the lowest priority. Can be overridden per run.
---@field parameters? aws.omics.RunParameters Workflow parameter names and values shared across all runs. Merged with per-run parameters; run-specific values take precedence when keys overlap. Can be overridden per run.
---@field storageCapacity? number The filesystem size in gibibytes (GiB) provisioned for each workflow run and shared by all tasks in that run. Defaults to 1200 GiB if not specified.
---@field outputUri? aws.omics.RunOutputUri The destination S3 URI for workflow outputs. Must begin with s3://. The roleArn must grant write permissions to this bucket. Can be overridden per run.
---@field logLevel? aws.omics.RunLogLevel The verbosity level for CloudWatch Logs emitted during each run.
---@field runTags? aws.omics.TagMap Amazon Web Services tags to associate with each workflow run. Merged with per-run runTags; run-specific values take precedence when keys overlap.
---@field retentionMode? aws.omics.RunRetentionMode The retention behavior for runs after completion.
---@field storageType? aws.omics.StorageType The storage type for the workflow runs.
---@field workflowOwnerId? aws.omics.WorkflowOwnerId The Amazon Web Services account ID of the workflow owner, used for cross-account workflow sharing.
---@field outputBucketOwnerId? aws.omics.AwsAccountId The expected Amazon Web Services account ID of the owner of the output S3 bucket. Can be overridden per run.
---@field workflowVersionName? aws.omics.WorkflowVersionName The version name of the specified workflow.
---@field networkingMode? aws.omics.NetworkingMode Optional configuration for run networking behavior. If not specified, this will default to RESTRICTED.
---@field configurationName? aws.omics.ConfigurationName Optional configuration name to use for the workflow run.
---@field sessionPolicy? aws.omics.SessionPolicy Optional inline policy json for scoping down permissions via a session policy on the IAM role provided in the roleArn parameter.
---@field engineSettings? aws.omics.EngineSettings Engine-specific settings for the workflow run. Use this field to specify configuration options that are specific to the workflow engine (for example, Nextflow profiles).
---@field scratchStorageMode? aws.omics.ScratchStorageMode Optional configuration for enabling scratch ephemeral storage mounted at /tmp. If not specified, this will default to SHARED. This configuration is applicable only for CPU tasks. For tasks using GPUs, scratch storage is always LOCAL.

